# TOOLING.md — template

Copy this to the root of your workspace (the same `workspace_root` you gave
setup) as `TOOLING.md`. The `claude-tooling-digest` hook injects the digest block
into every session automatically; the rest is read on demand.

**Keep the digest block under its line cap (`tooling_digest.max_lines`, 60 by
default).** Over the cap the block is **withheld entirely** — the session gets a
two-line overage notice and no map at all. That is deliberate: a block trimmed to
the cap reads exactly like a complete one, so a map can quietly lose its tail for
days. Demote rows into the body below the block rather than raising the cap; the
body is read on demand and costs nothing per session. **It is also withheld
past 9,500 characters of hook output**, however few lines it has: past ~10,000
the harness shows Claude only a 2KB preview. No setting moves that limit.

**The easy way is `/onboard`** — Claude copies this file and fills in the `TODO`
sections by *checking your machine*, which is most of them. Filling them by hand
works too.

**Why this file is yours and not in the toolkit.** It describes one machine and
one set of accounts. Which CLIs you have, which account your `gh` is logged in as,
which MCP connectors you have authorized — none of that is true on a different
machine. A fact copied into two places will eventually disagree with itself, so
keep each fact here once and link to anything canonical elsewhere.

Delete this header block once you've copied the file.

