**When a service has both a direct API and an MCP connector, decide per task,
and say which one you are using.** Neither is the default. Choose by what this
session actually has — its tools, credentials and network access, not the
surface's name. The API suits bulk, scripted or repeatable work, writes, and
anything the connector cannot do; the connector suits a quick interactive read,
or a session that cannot reach the API. Use one of them per task for the same
data, never both. Record a service-specific exception in the table above.

**⚠️ Flag any personal account with production reach.** Saying so here is what
makes it fixable later.

